Apply to `ash_authentication` on its 4.x line.

This adds a `sign_in_token_via_post?` option to the password strategy. When it is
set, `method_for_phase/2` returns `:post` for the `sign_in_with_token` phase
instead of `:get`, and the password sign in form hands its token over in a POST
body rather than a query string.

The return value stays a bare atom in every case. It never becomes a list, so
`AshAuthentication.Phoenix.StrategyRouter` on 2.17.3 and earlier keeps working:
that version stringifies a single verb and raises on a list. The two packages can
therefore ship in either order, and no version combination breaks.

The option defaults to `false`, so nothing changes until an operator enables it.

Apply with:

    git apply /path/to/ash-authentication-4x.patch

diff --git a/lib/ash_authentication/strategies/password.ex b/lib/ash_authentication/strategies/password.ex
